<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  wiredog-helper is a bare (non-bundle) Mach-O executable run as a root LaunchDaemon.
  It must claim NO entitlements here at all — not just no restricted ones.

  Confirmed empirically (VPN_CONNECTION_DEBUG.md Session 10): even
  com.apple.application-identifier / com.apple.developer.team-identifier alone (with
  zero restricted capability entitlements) caused taskgated-helper to reject every
  exec() attempt with "no eligible provisioning profiles found" (AMFI Code=-413). For a
  process launchd spawns as a root daemon, merely declaring an App ID makes AMFI require
  a matching provisioning profile — which, per Apple's own docs, a bare executable can
  never have. Signing this binary with a fully empty entitlements dict (as below) is what
  actually lets it exec on a clean machine. Do not add any entitlement here without
  re-testing on a genuinely clean machine first.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
